# Playwright E2E

## Run commands (never hide output)

- Use `npm run test:playwright` or `npx playwright test --reporter=line`
- **Never** pipe Playwright output through `tail`, `grep`, or `head` — it hides progress
- For one file: `npx playwright test tests/popup.test.js --reporter=line`
- For one test: add `--grep "test name"`

## Fail fast

- Fix the first failure before rerunning the full suite
- Config uses `maxFailures: 1` locally (see `playwright.config.js`)
- Do not retry locally; CI may use retries

## Speed

- Prefer `waitForSelector` over `waitForTimeout`
- Keep `waitForExtensionReady()` minimal — wait for UI markers, not fixed 3s sleeps
- Extension tests use `workers: 1` (shared browser context); do not raise without a fixture refactor

## Mock requirements

- Chrome storage mock must use **Promise-based** `chrome.storage.*` APIs (MV3)
- Authenticated flows must seed **Supabase `localStorage`** (`sb-<project-ref>-auth-token`) so `auth.getSession()` succeeds
- Patch **`navigator.onLine`** to `true` in init scripts — headless Playwright reports offline while routed fetch works; otherwise `AuthTokenRefreshHandler` queues ops forever
- Always override **`chrome.tabs.query`** in init scripts — real extension pages already have `chrome.tabs`; the default tab must be a normal https URL (not the extension page)
- Disable HTML5 `required` validation when testing JS validation messages (`form.noValidate = true`)

## When tests fail

1. Read the line reporter output
2. Fix root cause (mock, selector, or app bug)
3. Rerun the failing file before the full suite
